 },
 "lines": {
  "hook": "You just got buried by an avalanche.",
  "b1": "The snow stops, and it sets around you like concrete.",
  "b2": "You can't move. You can't even tell which way is up.",
  "b3": "Your warm breath melts the snow at your face, then it freezes into a mask of ice.",
  "b4": "Dug out within fifteen minutes, nine in ten people survive.",
  "b5": "After thirty five minutes, it's only about three.",
  "b6": "So rewind. Before the snow sets, remember three things.",
  "b7": "One. Get your hands in front of your mouth. That's your air pocket.",
  "b8": "Two. Don't spit to find which way is up. It's a myth. You can't dig out anyway.",
  "b9": "Three. Punch a hand up, so they can find you.",
  "end": "Save this. You won't have time to look it up."
 },
